   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 243153,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 38387,
    "poster_id": 4527,
    "post_rendered": "<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/5/f95d416af7bb18df958809b1b8150790a46a3728.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BU}{AB}=\\frac{CV}{AC}=\\lambda$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"124\" height=\"37\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/e/47e0810852e9fa56ffbc65106d7fcff323e79420.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle UBA=\\angle ACV$\"  width=\"134\" height=\"13\" > there for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/6/1c6b07c19608e8a01dc46bd0051787037d33c607.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta ABU \\cong \\Delta ACV$\"  width=\"139\" height=\"13\" ><br>\nit means that <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/f/aaf9333e12f92bd28ac006183ca65e95f1e23a01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta AUV \\cong \\Delta ABC$\"  width=\"139\" height=\"13\" >t</span>hen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/5/59516ad181d7ccf472b05b20ef388ae8f70085ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AV}{AC}=\\frac{AU}{AB}=\\frac{UV}{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"144\" height=\"38\" ><br>\nwe can get from this: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/5/78512bb15047e5495154765ee25991ca0d4fa625.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$UV,UQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" > are constant now<br>\n<br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfc9feb6b63c78f38bc0c6850c979961cb6d9c6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AQ=\\frac{\\sin \\angle B.QU}{\\sin \\angle QAY}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"141\" height=\"41\" > and it's constant so the locus of Q is a circle by center A.<br>\n<br>\nAmir",
    "post_canonical": "$\\frac{BU}{AB}=\\frac{CV}{AC}=\\lambda$ and $\\angle UBA=\\angle ACV$ there for $\\Delta ABU \\cong \\Delta ACV$\r\nit means that $\\Delta AUV \\cong \\Delta ABC$then $\\frac{AV}{AC}=\\frac{AU}{AB}=\\frac{UV}{BC}$\r\nwe can get from this: $UV,UQ$ are constant now \r\n\r\n$AQ=\\frac{\\sin \\angle B.QU}{\\sin \\angle QAY}$ and it's constant so the locus of Q is a circle by center A.\r\n\r\nAmir",
    "username": "Amir.S",
