    "poster_id": 1991,
    "post_rendered": "There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/3/6d3f8b726378d5420223c5cb14b10f24b202b187.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" > football teams in a round-robin competition where every 2 teams meet once. The winner of each match receives 3 points while the loser receives 0 points. In the case of a draw, both teams receive 1 point each. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/0/d10af8b3fc779f307fe5c87020e433b00a41801d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ k$\"  width=\"9\" height=\"12\" > be as follows: <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/b/4cbba381baa6bfb7e9f3edde1ba509ef4249f8d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ 2 \\leq k \\leq n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" >.</span>  At least how many points must a certain team get in the competition so as to ensure that there are at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6004b3c2a67fd6026215dd0bf8c1a00d15c6cdb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ k - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" > teams whose scores are not less than that particular team's score?",
    "post_canonical": "There are $ n$ football teams in a round-robin competition where every 2 teams meet once. The winner of each match receives 3 points while the loser receives 0 points. In the case of a draw, both teams receive 1 point each. Let $ k$ be as follows: $ 2 \\leq k \\leq n \\minus{} 1$.  At least how many points must a certain team get in the competition so as to ensure that there are at most $ k \\minus{} 1$ teams whose scores are not less than that particular team's score?",
