    "topic_id": 38391,
    "poster_id": 1991,
    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" > be a natural number greater than 6.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"12\" > is a set such that <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/c/b0c9216241d74eeaee927a8d360f6f5b2f356a18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|X| = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" >.</span>  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/5/7c5095e06bd8f0ddd4cb7bb1d1645254010aa862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"115\" height=\"16\" > are distinct 5-element subsets of <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"12\" >.</span>  If <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/9/5a98fe308dd51b37b95ee8c3a42c636769e34359.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &gt; \\frac{n(n - 1)(n - 2)(n - 3)(4n - 15)}{600}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"297\" height=\"38\" >,</span> prove that there exists <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/e/e9e7909a77c6b8e742934a6ea827481aabdba059.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{i_1}, A_{i_2}, \\ldots, A_{i_6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" > <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/f/77f48da021dbb986d47c031c4fa716606bb4cfa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1 \\leq i_1 &lt; i_2 &lt; \\cdots, i_6 \\leq m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"211\" height=\"18\" >,</span> such that <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/b/20bea792ae45bd28d06bfd6170715d673888cfe5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigcup_{k = 1}^6 A_{i_k} = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"86\" height=\"50\" >.</span>",
    "post_canonical": "Let $n$ be a natural number greater than 6.  $X$ is a set such that $|X| = n$.  $A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_m$ are distinct 5-element subsets of $X$.  If $m > \\frac{n(n - 1)(n - 2)(n - 3)(4n - 15)}{600}$, prove that there exists $A_{i_1}, A_{i_2}, \\ldots, A_{i_6}$ $(1 \\leq i_1 < i_2 < \\cdots, i_6 \\leq m)$, such that $\\bigcup_{k = 1}^6 A_{i_k} = 6$.",
