    "post_rendered": "There are 1997 pieces of medicine.  Three bottles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/9/299ddf7c0f03ea46bf09f81f93adeea0756aa15c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" > can contain at most 1997, 97, 19 pieces of medicine respectively. At first, all 1997 pieces are placed in bottle <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"13\" >,</span> and the three bottles are closed. Each piece of medicine can be split into 100 part. When a bottle is opened, all pieces of medicine in that bottle lose a part each. A man wishes to consume all the medicine. However, he can only open each of the bottles at most once each day, consume one piece of medicine, move some pieces between the bottles, and close them.  At least how many parts will be lost by the time he finishes consuming all the medicine?",
